<p>
  A <a href="https://github.com/basecamp/lexxy">Lexxy</a> editor synced with
  <a href="https://github.com/jpcamara/lexxy-realtime">lexxy-realtime</a>.
  Lexical stores its content in the Yjs document as nested
  <code>Y.XmlText</code> nodes. Each room is a <code>Room</code> record with
  <code>has_collaborative_rich_text :body</code>, and the page renders it
  with <code>form.collaborative_rich_textarea :body</code>, the gem's quick
  start. <code>LexxyChannel</code> extends the gem's
  <code>LexxyRealtime::DocumentChannel</code> and opens any room's body.
</p>
<p>
  After each update, the channel renders the room's whole body to HTML with
  <code>Y::Lexxy</code> and saves it to <code>body</code>, an Action Text
  field. yrby's tests check that this HTML matches what a live Lexxy editor
  produces. The panel below loads it over HTTP, so you can watch the saved
  HTML change as you type.
</p>
